'''Nuvo Vindi''' was a brilliant yet insane [[Gender|male]] [[Faust]] [[scientist]] who was employed by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. At the behest of the Separatists, Vindi re-engineered the [[Blue Shadow Virus]], an extinct virus capable of inflicting mass casualties across [[the galaxy]]. He worked out of a [[Trade Federation laboratory|secret laboratory]] on the [[planet]] [[Naboo]], where he attempted to spread the virus before being stopped and arrested by the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Jedi Order]].<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus" /> [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] were further able to find a cure on [[Iego]] in order to save those who had been infected in Vindi's laboratory.<ref name="Mystery Moons">{{TCW|Mystery of a Thousand Moons}}</ref> While in Republic [[Prison|custody]], Vindi, along with [[Lok Durd]], was part of [[Lieutenant Commander]] [[Orson Callan Krennic|Orson Krennic's]] original plans for a [[prisoner]] exchange with the Separatists to secure the [[Vallt Rescue Operation|release]] of [[Galen Walton Erso|Galen Erso]], [[Lyra Erso]], and the baby [[Jyn Erso]] from imprisonment on [[Vallt]].<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref>

==Biography==
{{Quote|Doctor Nuvo Vindi, the senior medic for the Perma families. He disappeared ten years ago.|Gregar Typho|audio=DrNuvoVindiSeniorMedic-BSV.flac|<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus" />}}
[[File:NuvoVindislaboratory.png|thumb|left|240px|Dr. Vindi examines his stockpile of the Blue Shadow Virus.]]
Nuvo Vindi was a [[Gender|male]] [[Faust]] from the [[planet]] [[Adana]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> who lived during the [[Republic Era|Fall of the Republic]]. He eventually became the senior medic for the [[Perma families]]. He then disappeared in [[31 BBY]].<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus" />

===Clone Wars===
Vindi then resurfaced ten years later in [[21 BBY]].<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus" /> He originally recruited by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist Alliance]] to create a virus that would target [[clone trooper]]s. However, he secretly pursued a more sinister dream: the re-creation of the deadly [[Blue Shadow Virus]].<ref name="Join the Battle" /> Vindi was given a [[Trade Federation laboratory|laboratory]] hidden on Naboo in its [[eastern swamps]] in which to perform his work. Vindi, being completely insane, did not have any moral qualms with recreating the virus despite its universal infection and mortality rate. Indeed he regarded the virus as a superior lifeform that had been "murdered" and viewed his recreation of it as passing judgement upon the galaxy and the supposedly superior lifeforms that had eradicated it.<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus" />

[[File:NuvoHolo.png|thumb|right|250px|Republic forces view a hologram of Vindi explaining his plot.]]
Vindi's experiments proved fruitful; not only was he able to re-create the virus, he subsequently modified it into an airborne strain, making it far more potent and dangerous than its previous waterborne form. He then had his droids manufacture [[Viral bomb|bombs]] with which he intended to load virus capsules into and then detonate in key Republic star systems. However, a small amount of the virus had leaked out of the lab and Vindi's tactical droid was then captured by the [[Royal Naboo Security Forces]] under Captain [[Gregar Typho]].<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus" />

Vindi then detected Naboo's [[senator]], [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] and representative, [[Jar Jar Binks]] approaching his lab. Vindi then sent his battle droids to capture them and bring them into the lab, where he showed them his plans for the virus as he loaded the last bomb and gave it to his [[LEP-series service droid|servant droid]], [[LEP-86C8]].<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus" />

[[File:Vindihastheruns.jpg|thumb|left|270px|Vindi flees his laboratory during the Republic assault.]]
When [[Jedi General]]s [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Anakin Skywalker]] arrived, accompanied by [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] and [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]], Vindi soon found his base under a Republic [[Raid on Nuvo Vindi's laboratory|attack]]. He used Amidala and Binks as hostages to bait the [[Jedi]], allowing him time to flee with samples of the virus. What he did not anticipate, however, was the Jedi's ability in catching up with him. [[Clone ordnance specialist]]s managed to defuse the virus bombs while Skywalker, with the help of [[shaak]] herder, [[Peppi Bow]], thwarted his escape and contain any virus leak.<ref name="Mystery Moons" />

==Personality and traits==
Nuvo Vindi was a Faust male scientist who was 2.07 [[meter]]s (6 [[Foot|feet]], 9 inches) tall,<ref name="Join the Battle" /> with [[Color|gray]] [[eye]]s and pale blue skin. He had large purple markings around his [[eye]]s and spoke [[Galactic Basic Standard|basic]] with a heavy accent. Vindi could be demeaning at times to the droids under his command, yelling at LEP-86C8 following the capture of Amidala and Binks. He was adamant in his belief that the Blue Shadow Virus was a life-form that had been murdered and was willing to torture and kill in order to revive it. His plot to release it back into the galaxy would have resulted in countless deaths, and Vindi showed no remorse at the thought. Instead, the doctor was genuinely excited, believing it would bring peace and purity to the universe.<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus" />

Vindi also stood undaunted, even with a [[lightsaber]] at his throat, after his defeat at the hands of the Jedi.<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus" /> The doctor was delighted at the thought of the virus escaping the lab and destroying Naboo, even if it was unable to get off of the planet. Furthermore, he enjoyed the prospect of not only the death of the Jedi, but himself as well.<ref name="Mystery Moons" />

==Skills and abilities==
Vindi had vast scientific knowledge and was proficient in genetic engineering.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Equipment==
Vindi was armed with a [[Weequay blaster pistol]] and had a pair of [[glasses]] which he held in place by hand. He also used viral bombs, that were filled with vials of the Blue Shadow Virus.<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus" />

